corridor":true,"resolution":"in the upwind corridor"},{"incident":"425776","entity":"Totalenergies Petrochemicals & Refining Usa La Porte Plant","rn":"RN100212109","start_local":"2024-06-29T16:40","compound":"Carbon Monoxide","pounds":2398.99,"facility_id":"110000619652","distance_km":5.9,"bearing_deg":149.2,"in_corridor":true,"resolution":"in the upwind corridor"}],"search_scope":"Searched every STEERS emissions event starting 07/01/2024 in Harris County (1 found; search complete). Also searched reports that started in the 30 days before and were still running (2 open that day; earlier search complete).","status":"reported_mismatch","incident":"425780","matched_facility_id":"110033536573","source_url":"https://www2.tceq.texas.gov/oce/eer/index.cfm?fuseaction=main.getDetails&target=425780","checks":[{"at":"T+24h","status":"reported","note":"initial notice filed 2024-07-01T08:37 local, 18.6 h after the reported discovery 2024-06-30T14:00"},{"at":"T+14d","status":"reported","note":"final report dated 2024-07-11, 9 days after the event ended"}],"compound_match":false,"reported":{"facility":"Air Liquide La Porte Asu And Smr","compound":"Carbon Monoxide","pounds":5690.0,"start_local":"2024-06-30T14:00","end_local":"2024-07-02T03:00","tz":"local (CDT)","cause":"Unit restart after shutdown due to a loss of steam to the process","match_basis":"ongoing (started 2024-06-30)","travel_h":1.97,"travel_speed_mph":4.7,"travel_distance_km":14.9,"start_to_spike_h":31.0,"arrival_local":"2024-06-30T15:58","spike_hour_local":["2024-07-01T21:00","2024-07-01T22:00"]}},"corridor":{"origin_site_id":"48_201_0036","half_width_deg":22.5,"max_km":15.0,"wind_from_deg":[138.0,150.0]},"packet":{"draft_en":"On July 1, 2024, the Texas state monitor at Channelview Drive Water Tower recorded 63.69 ppb of benzene in the 8:00 p.m. CST hour, against a 7-day median of 0.27 ppb. Wind there came from 150 degrees at 4.7 mph. 39 major permitted facilities lie in the upwind corridor. One of them, Air Liquide La Porte Asu And Smr, filed report 425780 for a release that started 2024-06-30 and, per the report, ran until 2024-07-02 03:00 local time, but the report does not list benzene, so it does not match this reading. Requested follow-up: confirm what caused this benzene reading.","draft_es":"El 1 de julio de 2024, el monitor estatal de Texas en Channelview Drive Water Tower registró 63.69 ppb de benceno en la hora de las 8:00 p. m. CST, frente a una mediana de 7 días de 0.27 ppb. El viento venía de 150 grados a 4.7 mph. Hay 39 instalaciones permitidas importantes en el corredor de donde venía el viento. Una de ellas, Air Liquide La Porte Asu And Smr, presentó el informe 425780 por una emisión que empezó el 2024-06-30 y que, según el informe, siguió hasta el 2024-07-02 03:00, hora local, pero el informe no incluye benceno, así que no corresponde a esta lectura. Seguimiento solicitado: confirmar qué causó esta lectura de benceno.","drafted_by":"template (deterministic, no AI)","guard":{"passed":true,"rejected":[]}},"cannot_say":["A matching report is not proof the facility caused every reading; other sources can add to a spike.","'Not yet reported' is not a finding about any facility: Texas requires a report only at or above a reportable quantity, and air readings cannot measure how much was released (30 TAC 101.201).","The upwind corridor comes from wind direction at one monitor (geometry only), not a dispersion model; it cannot tell facilities along the same bearing apart.","Facility coordinates are as published by EPA ECHO and may be approximate.","Only regulator-grade monitors whose data the state publishes are used (including two industry-funded Houston Regional Monitoring sites), never low-cost sensors."],"provenance":[{"file":"backtest/agc_2024_48_201_0069_45201.html","url":"https://www.tceq.texas.gov/cgi-bin/compliance/monops/agc_yearly_summary.pl","params":{"user_year":"2024","user_site":"48_201_0069","user_param":"45201","user_units":"ppb-v","report_format":"com